b (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T14:16:33-08:00","id":833517,"title":"","content":"If sounds kind of interesting, perhaps it could be a lot like Vampire the Dark Ages with mutated animals. Vampires and Supernaturals roam the world comparatively openly and rule little fiefdoms of humanity in exchange for protection and security. I could see a post atomic Zombie Apocalypse working just as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T19:48:43-08:00","id":833667,"title":"","content":"It would look horrible, because strampunk and dieselpunk are shallow &quot;genres&quot; that are little more than visual aesthetics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T20:24:30-08:00","id":833683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/832257-what-would-the-wod-look-in-an-alternate-steampunk-or-maybe-deaselpunk-universe?p=833667#post833667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would look horrible, because strampunk and dieselpunk are shallow &amp;quot;genres&amp;quot; that are little more than visual aesthetics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seriously, slapping a brass gear on something is not punk. It's an over romantic vision of industrial England.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T20:35:56-08:00","id":833687,"title":"","content":"I must respectfully disagree with both of you on this. steampunk and dieslepunk are more than an aesthetic as much as Gothic and punk are. they are a mood, a setting, a frame of mind that are just as legitimate a genre as Gothic Punk, just geared (pun absolutely intended) through a specific lens. it could work for world of darkness just as easily as Gothic Punk. and they are only called dieslepunk and steampunk as a derivative of cyberpunk steaming from a style of science fiction storytelling. which is kind of what we're aiming for on this. if it's not your thing that's okay, but at least let the rest of us enjoy it okay?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T00:49:58-08:00","id":834316,"title":"","content":"A steampunk version of the world of darkness in my mind would be a world where the sons of ether were far more successful in the 19th century than in the canonical world of darkness like instead of ether becoming disproved it was accepted as part of the consensus and just going by how the Mage books describe the first half of the 20th century could lend well a dieselpunk or atompunk setting specifically how World Wars 1 and 2 are described i don't know where exactly i read this but i remember something about an ethrite named reinholt i think it was building giant robots during WW 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":962,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/962-the-viking-anarch","user":"the viking anarch","date":". 02-21-2016, 03:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/962-the-viking-anarch","name":"the viking anarch","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T14:53:57-08:00","id":835402,"title":"","content":"A &quot;noirpunk&quot; WoD would be fabulous for a urban fantasy campaign, but not for a horror game. It would be &quot;Buffy vampire slayers meets Wild Wild West&quot;, or &quot;Monster High vs 1984 Big Brother's Dystopian world&quot;. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you wha